led.","id":"DF-SPECLANG-7","priority":"P2","reasoning":"Dogfood 2026-11-16, fresh clone (HEAD 2ace9a06), node v22.22.3 / npm 12.2.2, plain `npm install --no-audit --no-fund`. npm warns: \"1 package had install scripts blocked because they are not covered by allowScripts: better-sqlite3@12.11.1 (install: prebuild-install || node-gyp rebuild --release)\". After install there is no build/Release and no prebuilds/ under node_modules/better-sqlite3, and `new (require('better-sqlite3'))(':memory:')` fails with \"Could not locate the bindings file\" (require alone succeeds, so lint/tests that never open a DB do not catch it). package.json declares better-sqlite3 but carries no allowScripts/trustedDependencies, .npmrc is absent, and neither README nor GETTING-STARTED mentions the npm 12 remedy, so a fresh contributor silently gets a dead DB layer (dist/src/db/index.js:12 and the ralph-loop controller path). Note the bunker install leg runs `npm ci --ignore-scripts`, so the clean-machine fresh-install cell cannot see this class at all.","status":"pending","title":"P2 — fresh `npm install` on npm >=12 leaves better-sqlite3 without its native binding: DB layer unusable, repo declares no allowScripts","type":"bug"}
-{"acceptance_criteria":"Expected outcome: with the server started in one shell and `./bin/speclang stop` issued from another, the serving process exits 0 and prints no Error: ENOENT trace. Harness: start --port 39124, curl the dashboard for 200, stop, then assert the start process exit code is 0 and grep for ENOENT in its output is empty. Also covers stop-when-already-stopped (pid file absent) as a no-throw path with a unit test.","complexity":1,"created_at":"2026-11-16T06:52:26Z","detail":{"fingerprint":null,"metadata":{"provenance":"created_at stamped during provenance repair (row write was unpaired)","tick":"speclang-dogfood-2026-11-16-05-02-33"}},"id":"DF-SPECLANG-6","priority":"P3","reasoning":"Dogfood 2026-11-16, fresh clone HEAD 2ace9a06, node v22.22.3. Repro: `./bin/speclang start --port 39124` (serves HTTP 200, dashboard title SpecLang Dashboard), then `./bin/speclang stop`. The start process dies with an uncaught exception: Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory, unlink .speclang/daemon.pid, thrown at Module.unlinkSync (node:fs:1948:11) from process.shutdown (dist/src/daemon/index.js:70:12). Reproduced twice (ports 39123 and 39124). Cause: process.shutdown unlinks the pid file unconditionally, but `speclang stop` already removed it, so the still-live server throws on its own exit path and exits non-zero with a red stack trace. The daemon itself works (after stop, `daemon status` reports Stopped), so this is friction on every normal start/stop cycle rather than data loss.","status":"in_progress","title":"P3 — `speclang stop` crashes the serving process with an uncaught ENOENT on .speclang/daemon.pid instead of a clean shutdown","type":"bug","foreman_note":"wave dispatch tick SpecLang-foreman-2026-11-16-14-19-15: worker in own worktree (base origin/main 4c66e6fd)","worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/SpecLang-DF-SPECLANG-6","branch":"wt/DF-SPECLANG-6"}
